`mm` is checked for null/undefined **after** `render(data4Layout, svg)` and `setupViewPortForSVG(…)` have already been called. If there is no mindmap (e.g., an empty parse), the render is attempted with empty layout data and the viewport is still configured before the guard fires. Move the null check to before the render call:
```typescript
const mm = db.getMindmap();
if (!mm) return;
const data4Layout = db.getData();
// … rest of setup …
await render(data4Layout, svg);
```
